s to do that, with ready-to-run ideas. Tell me which you want me to perform (or share the files and I can run them for you).\\n\\nBest-practice comparison plan\\n\\n1) Byte-for-byte (binary) equality\\n- Why: confirms every bit is identical, including metadata, object order, compression, etc.\\n- How (command-line):\\n  - sha256sum file1.pdf\\n  - sha256sum file2.pdf\\n  - Compare the two hashes\\n\\n2) Metadata and properties\\n- Why: PDFs can differ in metadata even if visible text is the same.\\n- How (tools: exiftool, pdfinfo, pdftk):\\n  - exiftool -Title -Author -Creator -Producer -CreationDate -ModDate file1.pdf\\n  - exiftool -Title -Author -Creator -Producer -CreationDate -ModDate file2.pdf\\n  - Or: pdfinfo file1.pdf; pdfinfo file2.pdf\\n- Compare the outputs for any differences.\\n\\n3) Text content after extraction\\n- Why: ensures visible text extraction is identical; useful if fonts or encodings differ.\\n- How (tools: pdftotext):\\n  - pdftotext file1.pdf - | sort > t1.txt\\n  - pdftotext file2.pdf - | sort > t2.txt\\n  - diff -u t1.txt t2.txt\\n- Note: If you want exact line-for-line, skip the sort; differences in line breaks may show up.\\n\\n4) Structural/dudes diff at the PDF level\\n- Why: detects differences in object ordering, streams, or cross-reference tables.\\n- Tools: diff-pdf, pdfdiff, or qpdf --diff\\n- Example:\\n  - diff-pdf file1.pdf file2.pdf\\n  - Some tools will produce a visual diff image or a report of mismatched objects.\\n\\n5) Visual rendering diff\\n- Why: if both are visually identical, rendering differences may be negligible; useful to spot subtle rendering differences.\\n- How (render to images, then compare):\\n  - Convert first page to PNG: convert -density 150 file1.pdf[0] page1.png\\n  - Same for file2.pdf\\n  - Compare images: compare -metric RMSE page1.png page2.png null:\\n- Many environments provide tools like ImageMagick\\u2019s compare or perceptual diff.\\n\\nWhat I can do for you now\\n- If you share the actual PDF files (or allow me to access them), I can run a full set of these checks and report back:\\n  - Hash comparison results\\n  - Metadata differences (if any)\\n  - Text extraction diff\\n  - PDF-structure diff results (object-by-object or a summary)\\n  - Optional visual diff if you want\\n\\nIf you\\u2019d like, I can also provide a compact, ready-to-run script (bash or Python) that performs all of the above and prints a concise report.\\n\\nWould you like me to proceed with any of these steps? If you can provide the actual files, I\\u2019ll run the comparisons and summarize the findings.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"role\": \"assistant\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"parallel_tool_calls\": true,\n  \"presence_penalty\": 0.0,\n  \"previous_response_id\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_key\": null,\n  \"prompt_cache_retention\": \"in_memory\",\n  \"reasoning\": {\n    \"context\": \"current_turn\",\n    \"effort\": \"medium\",\n    \"mode\": \"standard\",\n    \"summary\": null\n  },\n  \"safety_identifier\": null,\n  \"service_tier\": \"default\",\n  \"store\": false,\n  \"temperature\": 1.0,\n  \"text\": {\n    \"format\": {\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    },\n    \"verbosity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\",\n  \"tool_usage\": {\n    \"image_gen\": {\n      \"input_tokens\": 0,\n      \"input_tokens_details\": {\n        \"image_tokens\": 0,\n        \"text_tokens\": 0\n      },\n      \"output_tokens\": 0,\n      \"output_tokens_details\": {\n        \"image_tokens\": 0,\n        \"text_tokens\": 0\n      },\n      \"total_tokens\": 0\n    },\n    \"web_search\": {\n      \"num_requests\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  \"tools\": [],\n  \"top_logprobs\": 0,\n  \"top_p\": 1.0,\n  \"truncation\": \"disabled\",\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"input_tokens\": 1655,\n    \"input_tokens_details\": {\n      \"cache_write_tokens\": 0,\n      \"cached_tokens\": 1408\n    },\n    \"output_tokens\": 2320,\n    \"output_tokens_details\": {\n      \"reasoning_tokens\": 1600\n    },\n    \"tota